tgenfunc19.pp	gap: MEASURED at compiler 1764cc174080 -- the reason here named a CLASS-HELPER rule that was already carved out (pasparser_decl.inc gates it on UClsHelperTk = tyClass) and was never this row's wall. TWO walls, both real, and the first is now fixed: `specialize DoTest<TTest>` with NO parentheses was refused by the call-site predicate (fixed 2026-09-06, the `(` was required for the keyword surface too). WHAT IS LEFT, line 32: the specialized body is spliced at the END OF THE USES CLAUSE, which precedes the program's own type section -- so `T` substituted by TTest2, a class declared in the PROGRAM, lands where TTest2 is not yet declared and reads `undefined variable (TTest2)`. CONTROL, measured: the same shape with the type argument declared IN THE UNIT compiles and prints the right answer, so it is the splice POSITION and not the substitution. bug-p-an-imported-generic-routine-is-spliced-before-the-programs-own-type-section
